// DRAFT (Act III, planning only). Ch20 U01 the release: Ilun (Teyo Marrin, the 50th Cantor, sixteen; vowbound §1).
// When he weakens he asks, in a BOY'S VOICE, whether Pila had a good life. If ch02_heard_pila Asha tells him (ninety-one
// years; Grandmother Osu is her granddaughter); if not, she says honestly that she doesn't know. He lifts either way.
// If ch18_haluna_lifted Asha adds that Haluna lifts its own now. The first goodbye that doesn't hurt. The net-float
// (the keepsake) is the last thing to go up. RULE 2: a release is the only thing that rises.
title: ch20_ilun_release
location: ch20/undertow_layers
---
@letterbox on
@camera U07
@music silence fade=1.0
@wait 2.0
Ilun as "Teyo" [worried]: Did Pila have a good life? #line:ch20_ilun_001 #tn:"Ilun speaks in the voice of Teyo Marrin, a sixteen-year-old boy. Pila is the little sister he sang in place of."
@wait 2.0
<<if $ch02_heard_pila>>
    Asha [tender]: She lived to ninety-one. Her granddaughter is the eldest in Haluna now. #line:ch20_ilun_002
    Ilun as "Teyo" [soft_smile]: Ninety-one. She'd have hated being old. #line:ch20_ilun_003
<<else>>
    Asha [sad]: I don't know. I hope so. #line:ch20_ilun_004
    Ilun as "Teyo" [neutral]: That's all right. I hope so too. #line:ch20_ilun_005
<<endif>>
<<if $ch18_haluna_lifted>>
    Asha [tender]: Haluna lifts its own now. Backs to the water. #line:ch20_ilun_006
<<endif>>
@music release_sting fade=0.0
@vfx glimmer_lift at=ilun count=40 motion=spiral_up rate=slow
@wait 6.0
@camera U08
@vfx glimmer_lift at=net_float count=1 motion=spiral_up rate=slow
@wait 4.0
<<set $ch20_ilun_released = true>>
@letterbox off
===
